<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rio de Janeiro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rio de Janeiro is a major port city on the south-eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. It became the seat of the Portuguese court in 1808 and then served as the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> throughout its existence. The Brazilian Empire profile notes that revenues from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> trade financed the modernisation of the city in the nineteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro.jpg" alt="Rio de Janeiro" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rafael Rabello de Barros · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cidade_Maravilhosa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
